# NOTE ON ANCHORING. A pattern with no slash in it (bin/, *.o) matches at any
# depth. A pattern that contains a slash (auth/server.key, var/log/) is anchored
# to the directory holding this .gitignore, so it would only match at the repo
# root and NOT under project/. Every multi-part pattern below therefore starts
# with **/ so that it matches at any depth as intended. This was a real bug:
# the key files were not being ignored at all.

# Build artifacts
bin/
*.a
*.o
*.d
build/
# macOS debug bundles (stale from earlier Mac builds)
*.dSYM/
.DS_Store
# Runtime state
**/var/log/
**/var/run/
# Local runtime config. sample.tetrishrc is the committed template; each
# checkout copies it to .tetrishrc and edits paths/ports locally.
.tetrishrc
# Secrets / generated keys. auth/generate_keys.sh IS committed - it is the
# deliverable that reproduces everything below from scratch.
**/auth/server.key
**/auth/server.crt
**/auth/cacsertificate.crt
**/auth/ca.key
**/auth/ca.srl
**/auth/server.csr
# Reference repositories (cloned as siblings, not committed)
application
networking
systems
# Tooling / harness state
.omc/